Snowdrake's Mom has an interesting history. While its original effect is sadly unknown (if it even had one to begin with), its stats were known, which were a solid 4/4/4. '''Alpha 2.1''' gave it the Magic to Paralyze all enemy monsters if you hand was empty. (This was noted as a buff.) But this was not used as much or at all in a [[:Category:Bravery|Bravery]] deck due to its passive, so '''Beta 5.3''' changed that to making it Paralyze them when your HP was at 10 or less, making it more useful against a [[:Category:Perseverance|Perseverance]] deck, which still blocked healing back then.

But this didn't stay long, as '''Beta 5.7''' reworked it again, as well as giving it its first stat change: increasing its cost by 1G. Now, instead of a certain requirement, Snowdrake's Mom will now always have a 50% chance to paralyze each enemy monster, making its ability work like that of [[Temmie]] at the time. This stayed until '''Beta 7.2''', where its ability changed again to paralyzing 2 random enemy monsters, at the cost of 7G. 

This stayed all the way until '''Beta 53.0''', where it returned to 5G, but also gained its first ATK and HP change, being -1 in both. In terms of effect, it was entirely reworked. Rather than having its effect work with Paralysis, it now gives +2/+2 to an [[:Category:Amalgamate|Amalgamate]] in your hand of your choice. But it also has a Synergy, which when activated, gives the chosen monsters +3/+3 instead. '''Beta 54.0''' gave it +1/+1, returning it to 4/4, at the cost of its Magic and Synergy giving -1/-1. 

